    %% CLASS DIAGRAM, PART 2 OF 2: DATA MODELS FOR THE 35 CURRENT USER STORIES
    %% Source: docs/user-stories.md.
    %% Part 1 (services) is UML_Class_Diagram.mmd.
    %% How to read this diagram:
    %% - Each model is one database table. The stereotype gives the table name.
    %%   The field names are the column names of that table.
    %% - Existing tables and columns: webapp/supabase/migrations/ (all files,
    %%   applied in order). `npm run diagrams` writes them between the
    %%   GENERATED markers. Do not edit that block, except to add a
    %%   [CHANGE x.y.z] tag at the end of a line. The generator keeps such tags.
    %%   A field that ends with ? can be null.
    %% - Proposed tables and columns: ER_Diagram_Proposed_User_Stories.mmd.
    %% - A class with the stereotype <<new ...>> is proposed. A proposed column
    %%   of an existing table is in a second block of that class below the
    %%   markers, with [NEW x.y.z]. Mermaid joins both blocks. When a migration
    %%   adds the column or the table, the generator removes the proposed item.
    %% - LegacyPerson (luperson) is shown because isSteward in queries.ts reads it.
    %%   The migrations make only id and email. The production columns are not
    %%   in the repository (see ER_Diagram_Legacy.mmd).
    %% - Legacy tables left out on purpose: sites_list_fnr,
    %%   sites_detail_fnr_test and sites_report_fnr_test. See ER_Diagram.mmd.
    %% - ActivityStats and SirSummary have no table. The server calculates them.
    %%   GET /api/profile returns ActivityStats as stats. US 1.0.5 (proposed for
    %%   Sprint 4) adds calculated metrics to it, not a points table. See
    %%   docs/user-model.md, "Gamification proposal".
    %% - INatObservation has no table. It comes from the iNaturalist API.
    %% - PdfOptions has no table. It is kept in S26_pdf_jobs.request_payload.
    %% - OfflineMapArea has no table. It is in the web app, in browser storage.
    %% - The FormResponse type in queries.ts also has naturalness_score,
    %%   naturalness_details and steward. They are not columns of
    %%   form_responses. getFormResponsesBySite reads them from the
    %%   answers of Q31, Q32 and Q13.

    %% BEGIN GENERATED: models
