    note for Site "US 2.0.4 (built): archiveSite sets archived_at and hides the Site. Nothing else changes.<br>permanentlyDeleteSite works only on an archived Site. It deletes the sites_pa row.<br>SIRs, attachments and homepage images stay with site_id set to null. S3 files stay.<br>site_stewards and site_page_fields rows go by on delete cascade. Person rows stay."
    note for SitePageField "US 2.0.5 and 2.0.10 (built): one row for each field of webapp/lib/sitePageFields.ts.<br>sapaa_website and inaturalist hold the Site links. A hidden field keeps its value."
    note for Attachment "US 4.0.6: the identifier column can already be null. The story changes the app validation.<br>US 7.0.8: an Attachment with response_id is owned by that SIR and is deleted with it."
    note for Person "activity_points exists, but nothing writes it. The US 1.0.5 proposal<br>calculates its metrics from form_responses and sites_pa (ActivityStats)."
    note for ProfileHiddenQuestion "user_id and GpxTrack.user_id are auth.users ids.<br>Person.auth_user_id links them to a Person. There is no FK between them."
    note for ProtectedArea "US 6.0.1: the KML import (webapp/utils/kml-import-actions.ts) upserts rows on (folder, fid).<br>sites_pa.protected_area_id is an optional link to protected_areas.id. Null means no link."
